DISCLAIMER

This package is an UNOFFICIAL community Linux port of the WorkBuddy domestic
client (https://www.workbuddy.cn). Tencent's official Linux package still
ships an older 5.6.x application than the current Windows release, so this
package combines the official Windows application payload with the Electron
runtime and Linux helper binaries from Tencent's official domestic Linux deb.

- WorkBuddy, WorkBuddy AI and CodeBuddy are products/trademarks of Tencent.
  This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Tencent.
- All application content is downloaded from Tencent's official servers at
  build time and is NOT redistributed by this package. The upstream software
  is proprietary; use of it is governed by Tencent's own Terms of Service and
  Privacy Policy.
- The app payload comes from the official Windows archive. Its app.asar is
  platform-neutral JavaScript, and this package removes the Windows/macOS
  binaries that cannot run on Linux.
- The Electron runtime, the bundled node/python session runtimes and the
  Linux CLI helpers (ripgrep, genie-trash, sandbox) come from Tencent's
  official domestic Linux deb. That Electron build carries the proprietary
  "workbuddyStorage" binding that sign-in depends on; stock Electron fails
  with CREDENTIAL_BOOTSTRAP_FAILED.
- Auto-update is non-functional on Linux. Upgrade by rebuilding this package.
- Known functional degradations versus the official Windows client:
  enterprise IM channels (the Windows-only native backend is unavailable, so
  the client falls back to the unavailable backend), the WeChat Pay plugin
  (no Linux build), and the Tencent Docs deep-collaboration engine (the
  official Linux SDK shipped by the deb is older than the Windows payload).
- When installed alongside the international port (workbuddy-intl-agent) both
  editions use the same ~/.workbuddy data directory and the workbuddy:// URI
  scheme. Run one at a time, or export WORKBUDDY_CONFIG_DIR to a different
  path for one of them, otherwise the single-instance lock and the profile
  database are shared.
- Do NOT report issues with this port to Tencent's official support
  channels. File issues with the community port project instead.
